# Lenovo IdeaPad D330 Detachable Keyboard Dock udev rules
# Detects pogo-pin dock insertion and removal events

# Hotplug (dock attach/detach) is handled by the tablet daemon USER unit's 3 s
# USB polling inside the graphical session. The system udev manager ignores
# ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}, and RUN+= would run as root with no session env, so
# neither can drive the user-session daemon.

# Intel HID Event Filter (INT33D5) tablet switch event binding
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Intel HID switches|Intel Virtual Button*", \
    ENV{ID_INPUT_SWITCH}="1", TAG+="systemd"
